   Environmental Management - Tourism, Society and Education Session,
   Tokyo, JAPAN, JUN 29-30, 2013},
Organization = {TU Bergakademie Freiberg; Tianjin Univ Finance \& Econ, Tourism Dept;
   Waseda Univ; German Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; IMRE Alumni Network},
Abstract = {Based on the literature review, the authors analyze urban residents'
   consumption preference of rural tourism through a questionnaire survey
   by taking Taizhou city as an example. Meanwhile, the development
   strategy of rural tourism in Taizhou is discussed. Researches of the
   author show that main motivations of urban residents to travel in rural
   areas includes relief pressure; go sightseeing; and enjoy delicious
   food. They have preference to local snacks, family camping tents and
   low-carbon transportation. In addition, tourism festival activities
   which made a mixture of local resources and culture were unique
   attractions to the tourists. But, they showed litter preferences to
   shopping. At the end of the paper, a couple of strategies are proposed
   to facilitate the development rural tourism based on urban redisents'
   preference, which include the diversified product development strategy,
   the word of mouth and new media marketing strategy.},
