Abstract = {The research emphasizes the validation for the Undergraduate Stress
   Inventory for the young Romanian Psychology students using behaviorally
   anchored rated scales as criteria. The aim of using behaviorally
   anchored rated scales is focused on measuring the behavior in
   academically environment working groups. The participants to the
   validation study were 385 undergraduate students of the Faculty of
   Psychology and Education Sciences, from the first and second year, age
   18 to 24 (M=20,43, A.S.=0,72), both males and females. The instrument
   was the Undergraduate Stress Inventory (7 dimensions). The results
   provide a 45.3\% reduction in the prediction error relative to using
   only the predictive model. Also, the predictive model highlighted
   variables: stressors within the academic environment, physical health,
   psychological health, anxiety, coping, positive emotions, negative
   emotions are predictors for the criteria (p<0.05). The conclusions
   highlighted that using behaviorally anchored rated scales measuring the
   behavior in academic environment working groups it is a proper way of
   validating Academic Inventories.},
