Organization = {Assoc Res Ctr Urban Underground Space; Sch Mining \& Metallurg Engn;
   Attiko Metro; S \& B; J \& P; OEMEAH; Planet Earth; MYTILINEOS Holdings},
Abstract = {This study consists in reporting a questionnaire for image of
   underground spaces in three countries showing different political
   situations, Japan, Korea and Indonesia. This paper introduces the
   difference and common points of them through the questionnaire. The
   authors mainly focused on the safety of underground spaces. The Japanese
   and Korean respondents recognized that they felt frightening many
   disasters there. The result shows the high rate of that the measures for
   the disasters are not sufficient among Japanese respondents comparing
   with the results of Japanese Koreans may consider that the measures in
   the underground spaces are relatively sufficient.\_The results of SD
   Method indicate several point; 1) the results of Japanese respondents
   are similar to those of Koreans. 2) Indonesian users feel ``Stronger,
   Cleaner, more Opening, Brighter, healthier than those of Korean and
   Japanese about against underground spaces. 3) Japanese and Kosraean
   respondents recognize the underground spaces as rather the perception as
   ``Crowded, Complicated and Quiet or Cold{''} than Indonesian ones.
   Japanese and Korean who have a negative image to the underground spaces
   may be due to the disasters such as fire, flood or earthquake damage at
   the subways or the underground spaces in Japan and the arson accident at
   Taegu Subway Station in Korea. These results will be useful indication
   planning and designing underground spaces in Indonesia.},
