   Univ; Univ Muenster},
Abstract = {Information about unplanned settlements in developing cities is often
   unavailable, despite their extent, which at times can dominate
   residential land-use. This research aims to contribute to the
   development of tools for monitoring such areas, by using spatial metrics
   as means for the identification of the morphology of unplanned urban
   settlements in VHR images. The methodology is tested in two case study
   areas: Dar es Salaam and New Delhi. The methodology builds on using
   image segmentation and on the assumption that segments representing
   homogenous urban patches are different in planned and unplanned areas.
   The morphological aspects (size, density and layout pattern) of planned
   and unplanned areas are analyzed using spatial metrics on segmented
   images. A final set of metrics has been used to build an `unplanned
   settlement index'. Comparison between results and land use data showed
   that the index can assist in the identification of unplanned
   settlements. (c) 2010 Published by Elsevier Ltd. Selection and/or
   peer-review under responsibility of Spatial Statistics 2011},
