   Buildings/3rd International Conference on Built Environment and Public
   Health, Guilin, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAY 29-31, 2009},
Organization = {Hunan Univ; Univ Hong Kong; Tsinghua Univ},
Abstract = {One province exhibition hall of World Expo Shanghai 2010 is presented in
   this paper, and two different air-flow distribution of the
   air-conditioning system in the province exhibition hall were simulated
   by FLUENT software, the first one is supplying air by openings on the
   ceiling, returning air through the side wall, the second one is
   supplying air by spouts on the side wall of 8m height, returning air
   through the side wall, the third one is supplying air by spouts on the
   side wall of 5m height, returning air through the side wall. And finally
   the optimized air-flow distribution is chose, which is based on the
   above simulated results of temperature field and air velocity field.
   According to the simulation results, the temperature field of the case I
   is more uniform, but the volume of the supply air is larger, the supply
   air is cooler, and the energy consumption will be huger, energy-saving
   is presented in case 2.Case 2 is the optimal air-flow distribution.},
