Organization = {Wexxex Inst Technol; Univ Cyprus; Univ Thessaly},
Abstract = {It is widely recognized that the use of fossil fuels causes
   environmental and geopolitical problems. It is essential that we turn to
   sustainable and regional ways of producing energy. Both producers and
   consumers are directed towards renewable energy. Traditionally, the
   strategy of Trias Energetica is used when sustainable energy becomes an
   integrated part of urban planning. Trias Energetica promotes three main
   concepts of sustainable energy production: to reduce use, use renewables
   and be efficient with the remaining resources.
   In the research area of Leuth, near the city of Nijmegen in the
   Netherlands, the Urban Harvest strategy has been introduced. In this
   strategy all available renewable energy sources are harvested. The
   outcome of the Leuth research is that the community applying the Urban
   Harvest strategy is theoretically easily able to fulfil its energy
   needs. The results are used to discuss Trias Energetica.},
