   Nagoya; Dept Planning \& Dev; Univ Thessaly},
Abstract = {Asia has been experiencing very high population growth and urbanization.
   Asian countries will witness a large population increase, which will
   have important implications for a variety of urban environmental issues,
   such as solid waste management. Nowadays, waste management is a major
   challenge in Asian countries, as it creates environmental problems. The
   present study reveals the problems and issues of solid waste management
   in Asian countries and certain important problems and issues that must
   be addressed in order to achieve public cooperation. At the core of the
   problems of solid waste management are the absence of adequate policies,
   enabling legislation, and an environmentally stimulated and enlightened
   public. This paper aims to identify parameters that help to explain the
   present situation and to assess the future amount of municipal solid
   waste (MSW) generated per capita in different Asian countries and how to
   develop an effective waste management strategy for Asian countries
   according to economic level.},
