   Earthquake and application for urban earthquake disaster prevention},
Booktitle = {Proceedings of the World Engineers' Convention 2004: Vol D, Environment
   Protection and Disaster Mitigation},
Year = {2004},
Pages = {643-647},
Note = {World Engineers Convention 2004, Shanghai, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV 02-06,
   2004},
Organization = {Shanghai Baosteel Grp Corp; Shanghai Automot Ind Corp; China Natl
   Petroleum Corp; China Petrochem Corp; State Grid Corp China; Shanghai
   Huizhong Automat Mfg Co Ltd; China Aerosp Sci \& Technol Corp; China
   Yangtze Three Gorges Project Dev Corp; China Natl Nucl Corp; BMW Grp
   Beijing; Chun Wo Construct \& Engn Co Ltd; Shui On Land Ltd; Air China},
Abstract = {In order to make effective use of geological and geotechnical data for
   urban earthquake disaster prevention, the authors studied the effect of
   deep geological structure and shallow ground to seismic damage in the
   1995 Southern Hyogo Prefecture Earthquake based on observed building
   damage and numerical simulation. The model for simulation consists of 2
   parts: the deep structure of the urban area of Kobe city is represented
   by 82D section and the shallow ground is modeled by 250m X 250m grids.
   Pseudo-spectral method and 1D dynamic analysis were employed for
   calculating ground motion. The result shows that the calculated ground
   motion (maximum acceleration and maximum velocity) agrees with the
   distribution of observed building damages in general, indicating that
   this method can be used for hazard prediction for earthquake disaster
   prevention.},
