Organization = {Natl Remote Sensing Ctr China; Assoc Environm Remote Sensing China; Comm
   Remote Sensing Geol, Geol Soc China; Comm Ocean Remote Sensing, Chinese
   Soc Oceanog; Comm Satellite Meteorol \& Space Weather, China Meteorol
   Soc; Comm Space Remote Sensing, Chinese Soc Space Res; Comm
   Photogrammetry \& Remote Sensing, Chinese Soc Geodesy; Photogrammetry \&
   Cartog Tech Comm Avion, Chinese Soc Aeronaut \& Astronaut; Comm Space
   Remote Sensing, Chinese Soc Astronaut; Comm Telemetry, Remote Sensing \&
   Control, Chinese Assoc Automat; Comm Software Ind, China Assoc Geog
   Informat Syst; Comm Remote Sensing, Chinese Hydraul Engn Soc; Affiliated
   Soc Land Informat \& Remote Sensing, Chinese Land Soc; Chinese Natl
   Comm, Int Soc Digital Earth United Remote Sensing Applicat Res Ctr
   Chinese Univ; Comm Environm Informat Syst \& Remote Sensing, Chinese Soc
   Environm Sci; Chinese Natl Comm Remote Sensing},
Abstract = {Using the inherent features of high resolution data, such as the shape
   and the texture, this paper proposed an object and rule based fuzzy
   classification method. First, multi-scale segmentations were used to
   obtain homogeneous objects at different scales. According to fuzzy
   classification ideas, these segmented objects were further classified by
   using the corresponding spectral, shape, texture, topology and other
   object-related characteristics. This method not only overcomes the
   limitations of pixel based classifications, but also takes advantage of
   the inherent features of high resolution data. To fully compare and
   analyze the proposed classification method, an IKONOS image of urban
   areas was selected as test data. According to four main classification
   steps, this data was classified as houses, roads, vegetation, and bare
   land. The classification results showed that the proposed method
   enhances the accuracy of classification and is of great advantages
   compared with the traditional pixel based classification methods.},
