   with symptoms?},
Booktitle = {PROCEEDINGS OF THE XV INTERNATIONAL CONGRESS OF THE INTERNATIONAL
   SOCIETY OF PSYCHOSOMATIC OBSTETRICS AND GYNECOLOGY},
Year = {2007},
Pages = {43+},
Note = {15th International Congress of the
   International-Society-of-Psychosomatic-Obstetrics-and-Gynecology, Kyoto,
   JAPAN, MAY 13-16, 2007},
Organization = {Int Soc Psychosomat Obstet \& Gynecol},
Abstract = {To explore the impact of migration on the perception of menopause and
   the use of hormone therapy a questionnaire was administered to 809 women
   all aged 45-60 years. This paper will present the findings from three
   target groups: 418 native German and 264 migrant women from Turkey
   living in Berlin and 281 women in Istanbul. To include illiterate women
   standardized face-to face interviews were also conducted. Compared to
   the native German sample, the results show more similarities among
   Turkish women in both cities (social and educational status, more
   reported menopausal complaints and less information received about
   hormone therapy). However, to cope with menopausal complaints Turkish
   migrant and German women in Berlin use and/or used more hormone therapy.
   Ease of access to the health care in Germany seems to be a decisive
   factor for the medicalization of menopausal Symptoms.},
