Note = {8th International Conference on Landscape and Urban Horticulture, ELECTR
   NETWORK, DEC 15-17, 2021},
Organization = {Int Soc Hort Sci, Div Landscape \& Urban Hort; Int Soc Hort Sci, Div
   Protected Cultivat \& Soilless Culture; Int Soc Hort Sci, Working Grp
   Urban Hort; Univ Catania, Dept Agr, Food \& Environm; Natl Res Council,
   Res Inst Terrestrial Ecosystems; Int Soc Hort Sci, Working Grp Landscape
   Hort},
Abstract = {With the development of urbanization, the problems of population health
   are increasingly prominent. It is found that urban green space plays a
   positive role in population health, and community green space is used
   most frequently, so its planning and design is of great significance.
   This study takes the green space in the community life circle as the
   research object. Theoretically, through literature induction, this paper
   summarizes the principles and strategies of community green space
   planning and design based on population health. Practically, taking
   Huilongguan and Tiantongyuan areas in Changping District of Beijing as
   examples for planning and design, and using ArcGIS for analysis, it is
   concluded that within the research scope, the coverage rate of a 15-min
   walk service range of the current park is 40.93\%, that of 10-min walk
   service range is 27.28\%, and that of 5-min walk service range is only
   18.12\%. The total amount of green space and park service coverage in
   the community life circle are insufficient, and the problem of blind
   areas is prominent. Two strategies are proposed according to the current
   situation. In terms of planning and layout, new regional community green
   space constitutes the core, and point community green spaces are added
   to stimulate community vitality; in terms of functional configuration,
   improve the quality and classify the existing green space.},
