Note = {International Workshop on New Developments on Sensors for Environmental
   Control, Lecce, ITALY, MAY 27-29, 2002},
Abstract = {Thick film gas sensors have been fabricated by screen-printing
   technology starting from different nanostructured semiconducting oxide
   powders both n-type and p-type. The temporal evolution of the
   conductivity changes in the thick-films have been studied in comparison
   with the concentrations of CO, NO, NO2, and O-3 measured by the
   analytical equipment. An atmospheric pollutant monitoring in an
   historical area through arrays of nanostructured thick film sensors is
   described. Quantitative responses of all arrays have been obtained by
   calibrating only one of them in the field and the others on the basis of
   the latter one.},
